DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x/5)^4)^5");
$fun_1 = Formula("(ln((x/9)))^4");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((-infinity, 13] - ((-infinity, 13] U {-10, 0, 5, 8}))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 16] U {-10, 0, 5, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((({-8, -2, 1, 3, 9})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -2, 1, 3, 9})) U (-infinity, 13]");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, -2, 1, 3, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -5, 5, 8, 9}) U {-8, -2, 1, 3, 9} U ({-10, -5, 5, 8, 9} U (({-10, -5, 5, 8, 9})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -2, 1, 3, 9}))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`1/14+11`]? [_____]{11.0714285714}
---

[`3+7+15*8`] is equal to [_____]{Real(130.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -2, 1, 3, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -5, 5, 8, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`(((A)) \cap A) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cap B \cup A \cup (B \cup ((B)) \cap A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, 0, 5, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 13\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 16\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - (B \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, 5, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -2, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -7, -8, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, 8>") x Compute("<6, 5, -4>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, -8, 3>") . Compute("<7, -2, 8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -8, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, 8>") x Compute("<-7, -8, 3>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, -8, 3>") x Compute("<6, 5, -4>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, 8>") . Compute("<6, 5, -4>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 4, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -10, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -2, 4, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, -10, -2>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 4, -1>") x Compute("<-8, -10, -2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 4, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 4, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
